Bugfix: Fix S3 backend silently stalling on stuck connections

Fix a bug where the S3 backend could silently stall for up to 55 minutes (2.4×
the watchdog timeout × 10 minio-go retries) when an S3/MinIO connection stalled.
The watchdog correctly canceled stuck requests, but minio-go's internal retry
loop treated the watchdog's timeout error as a generic, retryable I/O error
rather than as a context cancellation, so it always retried regardless of the
watchdog firing. This caused up to 10 silent retries, each with a new 5-minute
watchdog timeout, before any error surfaces to the user.

Restic now disables minio-go's internal retries (sets MaxRetries to 1) when the
backend-error-redesign watchdog is active, relying on restic's own retry layer
instead, which provides visible error reporting. This overrides any value set
via `-o s3.retries` while the watchdog is active.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22034
